    "text_full": "Skip to main content\nTurso home page\nSearch...\nCtrl K\nDashboard\ntursodatabase/turso\n18,893\nTurso Database (beta)\nTurso Cloud\nAgentFS (beta)\nTurso Homepage\nDiscord\nGitHub\nTurso Cloud\nIntroduction\nQuickstart\nLocal Development\nlibSQL\nLimitations\nMigrate to Turso\nDurability Guarantees\nPrivate Endpoints\nBYOK Encryption\nUsage & Billing\nAI & Embeddings\nEmbedded Replicas\nBranching\nPoint-in-Time Recovery\nSQLite Extensions\nDeprecated\nSDKs\nIntroduction\nAuthentication\nAuthorization\nSQL over HTTP\nOfficial SDKs\nCommunity SDKs\nCLI\nIntroduction\nInstallation\nAuthentication\nUpgrading\nHelp\nHeadless Mode\nCommands\nAPI Reference\nIntroduction\nQuickstart\nAuthentication\nErrors\nResources\nIntegrations\nVercel\nTurso Cloud\nQuickstart\n\nWelcome to Turso Cloud! Get started in minutes.\n\nCopy page\nDocumentation Index\n\nFetch the complete documentation index at: https://docs.turso.tech/llms.txt\n\nUse this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\n\nIn this quickstart you will learn how to:\nInstall the Turso CLI\nSignup to Turso Cloud\nCreate your first Turso Cloud database\nConnect to Database Shell\n1\n\nInstall the Turso CLI\n\nWe’ll be using the Turso CLI throughout this quickstart to manage databases and connect to the database shell.\nmacOS\nLinux\nWindows (WSL)\nbrew install tursodatabase/tap/turso\n\n2\n\nSignup to Turso Cloud\n\nThe next command will open your browser to sign up:\nSignup\nLogin\nturso auth signup\n\n3\n\nCreate a Database\n\nNow create your first database with the name my-db:\nturso db create my-db\n\nYou can inspect your new database using the following command:\nturso db show my-db\n\n4\n\nConnect to Database Shell\n\nCongratulations, you created a database! Now connect to it with the shell command:\nturso db shell my-db\n\nReplace my-db with the name of your database if you named it differently.\n\nCreate table\n\nInsert into new table\n\nSelect all rows from table\n\nWhen you’re ready to move onto the next step, you’ll want to to quit the shell:\n.quit\n\n5\n\nConnect your application to your database\n\nYou’re now ready to connect your application to your database. Pick from one of the SDKs below to continue:\nTypeScript\nRust\nGo\nPython\nAndroid\nSwift\nPHP\nRuby\nRuby on Rails\nC\nSQL over HTTP\n\nWas this page helpful?\n\nYes\nNo\nSuggest edits\nRaise issue\nIntroduction\nLocal Development\ndiscord\ngithub\ntwitter\nlinkedin\nPowered by\nThis documentation is built and hosted on Mintlify, a developer documentation platform"
